00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,537
22-爆音.

2
00:00:01,537 --> 00:00:03,051
The way she took up space.

3
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:06,829
The way she didn't look over her shoulder, terrified of who might be watching.

4
00:00:06,829 --> 00:00:09,060
If I took her back, I would kill this woman.

5
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:12,294
I would turn her back into the ghost who haunted my hallways.

6
00:00:12,294 --> 00:00:15,421
I would be the monster she had always painted me to be.

7
00:00:15,421 --> 00:00:16,709
I released the handle.

8
00:00:16,709 --> 00:00:20,814
I leaned back into the shadows of the seat, letting the darkness swallow me whole.

9
00:00:20,814 --> 00:00:22,945
The pain in my chest was absolute.

10
00:00:22,945 --> 00:00:25,369
It was a physical weight, crushing my lungs.

11
00:00:25,369 --> 00:00:28,104
It was the price of my sins."No," I said.

12
00:00:28,104 --> 00:00:34,226
Dante shifted in the front seat, twisting around to face me, his brow furrowed in genuine disbelief."Sir.

13
00:00:34,226 --> 00:00:36,295
We have a clear shot.We have the jet.

14
00:00:36,295 --> 00:00:40,585
We can have her home by morning." "I said no. "My voice was low.Absolute.

15
00:00:40,585 --> 00:00:43,561
I reached into my jacket pocket and pulled out a checkbook.

16
00:00:43,561 --> 00:00:50,274
I didn't hesitate as I scribbled a figure across the line-an amount that would make most men tremble, but meant nothing to me.

17
00:00:50,274 --> 00:00:53,993
"Go inside," I told Dante."Find the curator.Buy the painting.

18
00:00:53,993 --> 00:00:55,180
The one with the bird.

19
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,624
" "The bird, sir. " "Yes.

20
00:00:56,624 --> 00:00:59,834
Tell them it's for a private collection.Anonymous buyer.

21
00:00:59,834 --> 00:01:00,932
Then come back here.

22
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:06,730
" Dante hesitated, the instinct to argue warring with his training.Finally, he nodded."Yes, Boss. "

23
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:09,625
He stepped out into the downpour and crossed the street.

24
00:01:09,625 --> 00:01:13,858
I watched through the rain-streaked window, safe in the shadows of the tinted glass.

25
00:01:13,858 --> 00:01:18,186
I tracked Dante's movement as he entered the gallery and approached Casper.

26
00:01:18,186 --> 00:01:20,876
Then, I saw the moment that stopped my heart.

27
00:01:20,876 --> 00:01:22,212
Aurora turned her head.

28
00:01:22,212 --> 00:01:24,234
For a second, she looked out the window.

29
00:01:24,234 --> 00:01:31,347
Her eyes scanned the street, cutting through the gloom until they landed right on the black car.My lungs seized.Did she know.

30
00:01:31,347 --> 00:01:33,192
Could she feel me lurking in the dark.

31
00:01:33,192 --> 00:01:37,312
But her expression remained smooth.There was no fear.No recognition.

32
00:01:37,312 --> 00:01:40,461
Just a passing glance at a parked car on a city street.

33
00:01:40,461 --> 00:01:42,016
She turned back to her friends.

34
00:01:42,016 --> 00:01:44,614
She took a sip of wine.She had moved on.

35
00:01:44,614 --> 00:01:47,015
She had built a life where I didn't exist.

36
00:01:47,015 --> 00:01:51,001
Minutes bled by in agonizing silence until Dante returned.

37
00:01:51,001 --> 00:01:55,041
He slid into the front seat, bringing the scent of rain and cold air with him.

38
00:01:55,041 --> 00:01:56,323
"It's done," he said.

39
00:01:56,323 --> 00:01:58,106
"They'll ship it to New York next week.

40
00:01:58,106 --> 00:02:00,146
" "Good. " "Do we wait for her to leave, sir.

41
00:02:00,146 --> 00:02:04,058
Just to.confirm. " "No," I said, my throat tight."I've seen enough.

42
00:02:04,058 --> 00:02:06,641
" I looked at the golden window one last time.

43
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:07,836
I was the Underboss.

44
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:09,275
I was the King of New York.

45
00:02:09,275 --> 00:02:12,262
I had money, power, and fear at my fingertips.

46
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:17,200
But looking at the woman I loved, the woman I had driven away, I knew the truth.I was a pauper.

47
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,586
I had chosen my duty.

48
00:02:18,586 --> 00:02:20,100
I had chosen my honor.

49
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:24,688
And in the end, I was left with nothing but a painting of the freedom I had destroyed.

50
00:02:24,688 --> 00:02:26,414
"Take us to the airport," I said.

51
00:02:26,414 --> 00:02:31,123
The car pulled away from the curb, merging into the traffic.I didn't look back.I let her go.
